- `= 0` pure virtual
- Abstract class
- Subclass must implement
- Interface = all `= 0`

24.theory:
## Problem

```cpp
class Animal { public: ~Animal() {} };
class Dog : public Animal {
    int* data;
public:
    Dog() : data(new int[100]) {}
    ~Dog() { delete[] data; }
};

Animal* a = new Dog();
delete a;   // only ~Animal → leak
```

## Solution

```cpp
class Animal {
public:
    virtual ~Animal() = default;
};
```

Virtual destructor — correct dtor on delete via base pointer.

## Rule

If class is for inheritance (has virtual functions) — virtual destructor mandatory.

## Summary

- `virtual ~ClassName() = default;`
- Required with inheritance
- All interfaces — virtual dtor
- Without — leak

