41.theory:
## Putting together

Course covered: syntax, refs, classes, inheritance, polymorphism, STL, lambdas, smart pointers, exceptions, templates.

## Final example

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>
#include <numeric>

class Product {
    std::string name_;
    double price_;
public:
    Product(std::string name, double price)
        : name_(std::move(name)), price_(price) {}
    const std::string& name() const { return name_; }
    double price() const { return price_; }
};

int main() {
    std::vector<Product> products = {{"A", 100}, {"B", 200}, {"C", 50}};
    double total = std::accumulate(products.begin(), products.end(), 0.0,
        [](double s, const Product& p) { return s + p.price(); });
    std::cout << "Sum: " << total << "\n";

    auto it = std::find_if(products.begin(), products.end(),
        [](const Product& p) { return p.price() > 150; });
    if (it != products.end())
        std::cout << "Expensive: " << it->name() << "\n";
}
```

## Checks

- class + private + ctor + const getters
- `std::vector`, `accumulate`, `find_if`
- Lambdas
- Structured bindings

## What if

- No `const` getter — fails on const object
- `it == end()` unchecked — UB

## Summary

- class + STL + algorithms + lambdas
- Compose: sort → filter → accumulate
- Smart pointers for polymorphism
- Check `end()`
